Three sites on a lake, measured on the

96
00:04:06,580 --> 00:04:07,500
same day.

97
00:04:07,780 --> 00:04:09,460
Read one column at a time.

98
00:04:09,940 --> 00:04:12,980
Nitrate and phosphate rise from A to C,

99
00:04:13,020 --> 00:04:15,620
and site B already has about nine times

100
00:04:15,700 --> 00:04:16,900
the phosphate of A.

101
00:04:17,140 --> 00:04:19,940
Dissolved oxygen falls from eight point four to

102
00:04:20,020 --> 00:04:22,100
three point nine milligrams per litre.

103
00:04:22,500 --> 00:04:26,260
And the observations agree: clear water, then scum,

104
00:04:26,340 --> 00:04:27,300
then dead fish.

105
00:04:27,700 --> 00:04:29,940
So C shows the strongest signs of an

106
00:04:29,980 --> 00:04:33,020
oxygen problem, and B also needs follow-up.

107
00:04:33,220 --> 00:04:35,180
What the table can't show is what the

108
00:04:35,220 --> 00:04:36,740
oxygen does at night.

109
00:04:37,967 --> 00:04:39,406
So why monitor?

110
00:04:39,887 --> 00:04:42,926
A number only means something against a guideline

111
00:04:42,967 --> 00:04:44,126
for that water's use.

112
00:04:44,607 --> 00:04:47,486
For drinking water, the nitrate guideline is fifty

113
00:04:47,647 --> 00:04:51,006
milligrams per litre, set to protect babies, but

114
00:04:51,087 --> 00:04:53,486
far lower nutrient levels can feed a bloom

115
00:04:53,527 --> 00:04:54,406
in a river.

116
00:04:54,767 --> 00:04:57,326
Sampling above and below a source finds where

117
00:04:57,367 --> 00:05:00,486
the nutrients enter, and that decides the fix.

118
00:05:00,767 --> 00:05:03,166
Monitoring also tells a treatment plant what it

119
00:05:03,247 --> 00:05:05,646
has to remove, like algae at a drinking

120
00:05:05,727 --> 00:05:08,766
water intake, or nitrogen and phosphorus in sewage

121
00:05:08,847 --> 00:05:09,886
before it's released.

122
00:05:10,367 --> 00:05:13,406
And after any fix, only measurement shows whether

123
00:05:13,447 --> 00:05:14,606
the water recovered.

